Whitespace-bearing values round-trip through the file rather than being mangled or
rejected: a tab lands as a double-quoted escape and a newline as a folded single-quoted
block, each reloading as the text that was given. The newline arrives through a Jinja string
literal since a command line cannot carry a raw one.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
---
# Body
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md summary='hello	world' 'lined={{ "x\ny" }}'

-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
--- plan.md
+++ plan.md
@@ -1,4 +1,8 @@
 ---
 title: Foo
+summary: "hello\tworld"
+lined: 'x
+
+  y'
 ---
 # Body
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: summary=hello	world, lined=x
y
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
summary: "hello\tworld"
lined: 'x

  y'
---
# Body
